  "helpTitle": "How to play",
  "helpReplay": "Show the tutorial again",
  "help_goal_t": "Goal",
  "help_goal": "The stopwatch counts seconds. Tap the screen when it shows 5.00 — the closer, the better:\n• 5.00 (±0.010 s): a PERFECT plus a bonus — seconds of your clocks' work\n• PERFECT (±0.015 s): 6 Ticks, streak +3\n• GREAT (±0.030 s): 3 Ticks, streak +2\n• GOOD (±0.050 s): 1 Tick, streak +1\n• CLOSE (±0.150 s): a small consolation, the streak breaks\nAnything further is a miss. A tap over a second before the target counts as a slip and is ignored. Skills widen the windows (except 5.00).",
  "help_tiki_t": "Ticks",
  "help_tiki": "Ticks are the game's money. The big counter at the top shows how many you have, the smaller one below it how much you earn per second. You spend them in the shop at the bottom.",
  "help_clocks_t": "Clocks",
  "help_clocks": "Clocks (the Clocks tab) play for you and add Ticks every second — even while the game is closed. Grandpa comes first; buying a clock reveals the next, stronger one. The number on the icon is how many you own. ×1, ×10, ×100 and MAX set how many you buy at once.",
  "help_upgrades_t": "Clock bonuses",
  "help_upgrades": "Each clock has a bar. Once you own as many as it shows (10, 20, 40… for Grandpa), all clocks of that kind earn more — free, on their own. The first clocks get ×2; pricier ones have lower counts and a smaller multiplier. Own 25 each of two clocks that go together (like Grandpa and Grandma) and a synergy switches on: they boost each other.",
  "help_skills_t": "Skills",
  "help_skills": "Skills (the Skills tab) boost your own hits: bigger rewards, wider windows, longer streaks. They have levels — \"Level 2/10\" means the second of ten. Tap a card to read the details.",
  "help_combo_t": "Streak (combo)",
  "help_combo": "Hits in a row build a streak, and the streak multiplies every payout (the COMBO bar under the clock). A miss resets it, unless you have a Shield.",
  "help_golden_t": "Golden Second",
  "help_golden": "Every so often (10 minutes on average) a golden clock flies across the screen. Tap it and the next round turns golden. Hit that round and you get one of the bonuses; the better the hit, the stronger it is (PERFECT in full, GREAT 60%, GOOD 30%, a miss nothing):\n• Frenzy (45% chance): all income — clocks and hits — ×7 for 77 s\n• Lucky (45%): Ticks at once — 10 minutes of your clocks' work\n• Hot hand (10%): for 60 s every hit counts as a PERFECT and pays ×10",
  "help_modes_t": "Toggles",
  "help_modes": "Later, toggles appear above the shop: \"Blind\" (from 4.00 the stopwatch and its ring disappear, but hits pay ×3, ×4 with the Daredevil perk), \"Second clock\" (two stopwatches, each half of the screen is one) and \"Auto buyer\" (buys clocks for you).",
  "help_season_t": "Events",
  "help_season": "On holidays the golden clock changes its look. The badge at the top shows your progress: how many holiday clocks you caught (e.g. 0/5) and how many hits you made (e.g. 0/50). Finishing pays a reward.",
  "help_prestige_t": "Time paradox",
  "help_prestige": "Once you've collected a lot, the swirl at the top lights up. You can then rewind time: you start over but get Chronons — a permanent bonus to everything, so the next run goes much faster — and as many Time shards ✦. Spend the Shards on perks right after rewinding, before the new run starts, or later on the paradox screen.",
  "help_icons_t": "Icons at the top",
  "help_icons": "Trophy — achievements (each gives +1% income). Chart — statistics. Gear — settings. Swirl — time paradox. Question mark — this help.",
